configs: nanopi-r3s-rk3566: enable SPL_GZIP for gzip-compressed FIT loadables

rkbin's FIT image for this board ships its non-TPL loadables (ATF/
BL31, OP-TEE) gzip-compressed to fit within SPL's size/time budget.
common/spl/spl_fit.c only attempts decompression when
spl_decompression_enabled() is true, which in turn requires
CONFIG_SPL_GZIP (or CONFIG_SPL_LZMA) to be enabled - without it,
compressed loadables are copied into RAM as-is and never inflated,
so any component encoded as IH_COMP_GZIP fails to boot correctly.

Note: an earlier version of this patch also added
CONFIG_SPL_OPTEE_IMAGE=y to enable OP-TEE registration in SPL. That
option was dropped again: its only implementation,
common/spl/spl_optee.S, is written entirely in ARM32 assembly
(.syntax unified, "mov pc, r3") and fails to assemble on this
board's AArch64 target. On this board OP-TEE is handed to BL31 via
the ATF path in common/spl/spl_atf.c instead (CONFIG_SPL_ATF=y is
already enabled), which does not depend on CONFIG_SPL_OPTEE_IMAGE at
all - see 202-image-optee-alias.patch for the actual fix needed on
that path (the FIT "os" string alias).

--- a/configs/nanopi-r3s-rk3566_defconfig
+++ b/configs/nanopi-r3s-rk3566_defconfig
@@ -71,3 +71,4 @@ CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_DWC3=y
 CONFIG_USB_DWC3_GENERIC=y
 CONFIG_ERRNO_STR=y
+CONFIG_SPL_GZIP=y
